        "requirements_title": "Upgrade and New Installation of Intrusion Detection System (IDS)",
        "requirement": "This Statement of Work (SOW) provides for the upgrade of existing analog IDS panels to Internet Protocol (IP)-based digital alarm control panels and the installation of new standalone IP-based IDS systems in offices that currently do not have an IDS installed. All new IDS installations and panel upgrades shall include an IP alarm control panel, a minimum of one (1) keypad, a compatible locking metal enclosure, and all appurtenances necessary to provide a complete, fully functional IDS. Depending on site-specific conditions and network availability, the Contractor may be required to install a wireless point-to-point transceiver to support communications.\r\n\r\nThe alarm control panel shall support two-way network-based communications for system monitoring, alarm reporting, programming, diagnostics, and maintenance activities.\r\n\r\nThe Vendor shall replace existing IDS components, sensors, and end devices with current-generation IDS equipment that is fully compatible with the newly installed IP-based alarm control panel. The completed system shall be delivered as a fully operational, turnkey IDS solution.\r\n\r\nThe IDS shall operate independently of the GSA Enterprise Physical Access Control System (EPACS). The Contractor shall integrate the IDS with the FPS-approved Gallagher EPACS platform at the time of installation.",
